&lt;h2&gt;Why join us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll play an important role in supporting revenue accounting quality, financial reporting accuracy and revenue recognition compliance within a global finance organisation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building an inclusive and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h1&gt;Senior Revenue Accountant&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location, UK, Manchester, (Hybrid)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Inizio&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inizio is a global partner to health and life sciences organisations, delivering specialist expertise across the product and patient journey. Through Global Finance Services (GFS), we provide high-quality, efficient and compliant finance operations that support business performance worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Global Revenue Controller, we are seeking a Senior Revenue Accountant to support revenue accounting activities within our Global Finance Services (GFS) shared services organisation, acting as a subject matter expert across complex revenue recognition, accrued and deferred revenue positions and period-end close. You will be responsible for delivering accurate and timely revenue accounting processes, ensuring compliance with revenue recognition standards, maintaining the integrity of revenue-related balance sheet accounts and supporting high-quality financial reporting.&lt;br&gt;Working closely with GFS RTR and OTC teams, you will perform core revenue accounting activities, support period-end close, investigate accounting issues and contribute to the effective delivery of the end-to-end Order to Cash process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Here&#39;s what you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Revenue Accounting &amp;amp; Financial Close&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and process revenue accounting journals and financial transactions in accordance with applicable accounting standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform reconciliations for accrued revenue, deferred revenue, contract liability and related balance sheet accounts, driving timely clearance of aged or complex reconciling items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply revenue recognition policies to assigned contracts in accordance with IFRS 15 or applicable standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile revenue ledger postings to billing system data and investigate variances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead month-end, quarter-end and year-end close activities, including cut-off reviews and period-end adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate revenue accounting records, contract schedules and supporting documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with preparation of revenue reporting schedules and supporting information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate routine revenue accounting issues and escalate complex matters where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Global Revenue Controller in the delivery of revenue accounting, governance and financial control objectives, and share knowledge and good practice with peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Governance&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GFS RTR, OTC and Group Finance teams to resolve revenue accounting issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit activities by providing documentation and responding to information requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with accounting policies, internal controls and governance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Continuous Improvement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to process improvement initiatives and operational excellence activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve efficiency, data quality and revenue accounting processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree (or equivalent professional qualification) in Accounting, Finance, Commerce or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified ACA, ACCA, CIMA or equivalent required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 – 6 years&#39; experience in revenue accounting within a global Shared Services Centre (SSC) or Global Business Services (GBS) environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting revenue recognition, reconciliations, journal processing and month-end close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Operational Expertise&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of revenue recognition standards (IFRS 15 or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using ERP systems such as Oracle Fusion or similar accounting platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Microsoft Excel skills including lookups, pivot tables and reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding financial controls, compliance and reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Problem Solving &amp;amp; Innovation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate reconciliation differences, revenue recognition issues and data quality exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve routine accounting issues independently while escalating complex matters appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support improvements to accounting processes and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build effective relationships with Finance, Commercial teams and other internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly regarding revenue accounting queries and reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively across the shared services organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Performance, Impact &amp;amp; Ways of Working&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and commitment to accounting accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet period-end deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative team player focused on delivering accurate financial information and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why join us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll play an important role in supporting revenue accounting quality, financial reporting accuracy and revenue recognition compliance within a global finance organisation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building an inclusive and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h1&gt;Senior Accountant&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: UK, Manchester ( Hybrid)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Inizio&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inizio is a global partner to health and life sciences organisations, delivering specialist expertise across the product and patient journey. Through Global Finance Services (GFS), we provide high-quality, efficient and compliant finance operations that support business performance worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Divisional Controller, we are seeking a Senior Accountant to lead accurate and timely period-end close activities within our Global Finance Services (GFS) shared services organisation. You will act as a subject matter expert across Record-to-Report (RTR) processes including journal preparation, balance sheet reconciliations, intercompany accounting and variance analysis while driving accounting quality, financial control and continuous improvement. Working closely with finance stakeholders, you will support governance, audit readiness and the development of junior team members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Here&#39;s what you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Financial Accounting &amp;amp; Close&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform and oversee complex accounting activities, reconciliations and financial reporting support processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key balance sheet accounts and ensure timely reconciliation and resolution of outstanding items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and sign off bank reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee intercompany accounting and resolution of differences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead assigned month-end, quarter-end and year-end close activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review accounting transactions and escalate issues where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review variance analysis, providing clear commentary on movements in assigned balance sheet accounts and period-end results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review schedules and supporting information for internal and external reporting requirements, ensuring accuracy and completeness ahead of submission deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Governance &amp;amp; Controls&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support reporting requirements, accounting policy implementation and process changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve accounting processes, controls and reporting quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Divisional Controller in delivering accounting, governance and financial control objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and support Accountants in the execution of accounting activities and capability development; this is not a line management responsibility but carries an expectation of technical leadership and work review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree (or equivalent professional qualification) in Accounting, Finance, Commerce or related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified ACA, ACCA, CIMA or equivalent preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–8 years&#39; progressive finance experience including financial accounting, reconciliations, intercompany accounting, close activities, audit support and financial controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within a global Shared Services Centre (SSC) or Global Business Services (GBS) environment is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Technical &amp;amp; Operational Expertise&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ERP experience (Oracle Fusion or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Microsoft Excel skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong accounting standards, financial reporting and balance sheet management knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of internal controls and SOX or equivalent governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting process improvement or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Problem Solving &amp;amp; Innovation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve complex reconciliations, intercompany disputes and accounting issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply judgement to non-routine transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process improvements and control enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build effective relationships with Finance, Tax, Treasury, Audit and Divisional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate technical accounting matters clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Performance, Impact &amp;amp; Ways of Working&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and strong organisational skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, proactive and committed to continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why join us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll play a key role in delivering high-quality financial reporting and strengthening accounting controls across Global Finance Services while supporting continuous improvement and operational excellence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;elementToProof&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every job requirement? That&#39;s okay! Our company is dedicated to building an inclusive and authentic workplace. If you&#39;re excited about this role, but your experience doesn&#39;t perfectly fit every qualification, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right person for this role or others.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Banyan Software is the best permanent home for software businesses that serve specialized industries, their employees, and their customers. We are on a mission to acquire, build, and grow great companies worldwide, helping them modernize through shared AI expertise and operational discipline. The Banyan Software Foundation, endowed with $100 million in Banyan stock, leverages technology to build a greener and more equitable world. Banyan is Great Place to Work Certified, a five-time Inc. 5000 honoree, and a top 10 company on the Deloitte Technology Fast 500. Founded in 2016 and headquartered in Atlanta, Banyan operates more than 100 portfolio companies across North America, the UK, EU, and APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Banyan Software is the best permanent home for software businesses that serve specialised industries, their employees, and their customers. We are on a mission to acquire, build, and grow great companies worldwide, helping them modernise through shared AI expertise and operational discipline. The Banyan Software Foundation, endowed with $100 million in Banyan stock, leverages technology to build a greener and more equitable world. Banyan is a Great Place to Work Certified company, a five-time Inc. 5000 honoree, and a top-10 company on the Deloitte Technology Fast 500. Founded in 2016 and headquartered in Atlanta, Banyan operates more than 100 portfolio companies across North America, the UK, the EU, and APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About WIZE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WIZE is the leading all-in-one Portfolio Management System for Swiss boutique wealth managers, External Asset Managers, and family offices. Founded in Geneva in 2010, WIZE has earned a trusted position in a relationship-driven market through deep product capability and a differentiated back-office outsourcing service that competitors have not replicated. The company operates on a highly recurring subscription model, holds a strong position within its vertical, and is in excellent operating shape. WIZE is now entering its first chapter of international ownership under Banyan Software, combining more than fifteen years of product depth and client trust with the operational and AI expertise of a global software group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join WIZE directly as Managing Director,&amp;nbsp; United Kingdom, reporting to the CEO of WIZE, with responsibility for establishing and growing the UK business. This is a value-creation mandate, not a turnaround. . You will take the business into a new market, with the United Kingdom as the primary prize. The product has to remain the primary competitive advantage, the recurring revenue base has to be protected, and the opportunity to create structural distance through AI is real.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the UK client and partner relationships, build the commercial motion from the ground up, and partner with the CEO and product and technology leader to ensure the platform addresses the needs of the UK market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have substantial authority over the execution of the agreed UK strategy. Key commercial development decisions, including market positioning, target segments, pricing, partnerships, resource allocation, and major commercial commitments, will be decided jointly with the CEO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will do this with the long-term backing of a permanent-capital owner, free from the pressure to flip the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial &amp;amp; Revenue Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the foundation of the UK subsidiary and work closely with the CEO to define WIZE&#39;s expansion into the UK market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the execution of WIZE&#39;s UK strategy, market positioning, and competitive response in the wealth management software market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive UK revenue and ARR growth with direct accountability across new customer acquisition, expansion, pricing execution, and the development of recurring revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute the UK go-to-market motion from the ground up: local presence, bank and partner relationships, and a repeatable pipeline where little exists today.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary executive relationship owner for key UK clients, bank partners, and influencers, ensuring high levels of client satisfaction, retention, and contract renewal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deepen strategic partnerships across private banks, discretionary fund managers, and the wider UK wealth management ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate client needs and proactively identify opportunities to expand the company&#39;s footprint within existing UK&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify AI-driven opportunities to reposition the product and create durable competitive distance within the WealthTech vertical, working with the CEO and product and technology leader to assess and prioritise them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Technology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the needs of the UK market in product roadmap discussions, ensuring that market feedback reflects the needs of boutique wealth managers and the competitive dynamics of the Portfolio Management Systems market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a credible AI roadmap. AI must be embedded as a genuine operational and product advantage, not a roadmap line item.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion AI-first product thinking, identifying where automation, predictive insights, and intelligent workflows create durable differentiation for UK clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the CEO and CPTO so that the roadmap, packaging, and pricing tiers align tightly with UK commercial needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather structured feedback from UK prospects, clients, and partners and translate it into clear commercial and product recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and implement the UK commercial development strategy jointly with the CEO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the UK financial performance, budgeting, and resource allocation to ensure sustainable profitability. Prepare and manage the UK commercial budget and resource plan, subject to approval by the CEO and Chief Revenue Officer, to ensure sustainable growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage risk across operations, contracts, and market dynamics; respond decisively to changes in the competitive or regulatory landscape&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a high-performing UK sales team, elevating talent density and making hard calls on underperformance with speed and directness, while protecting the trust-based culture that makes WIZE what it is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish decision rights, execution cadences, and accountability frameworks that enable the business to sustain higher growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and proactively with the CEO on business performance, strategic priorities, pipeline development, and market conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closely with WIZE&#39;s Geneva-based product, technology, implementation, client service, compliance, and operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Are Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Managing Director we are looking for is a commercially-led WealthTech operator with deep roots in the UK wealth management software market who leads with an AI-first mindset and is energised by the opportunity to create real, lasting business value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have personally owned a revenue number, built a commercial motion where none existed, and opened a new geography from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have held senior commercial responsibility at a software company serving wealth managers, private banks, or asset managers, with a track record of treating product as a primary strategic lever, closing complex, relationship-driven deals at a senior level, and leading your organisation through at least one meaningful inflexion point.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You proactively reposition ahead of market pressure, make difficult commercial and talent decisions for the long-term health of the business, and understand how to grow recurring revenue and protect the retention that sustains durability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a value-creating enterprise SaaS leader who sees AI not as a feature but as a structural advantage embedded in how they sell, operate, and create enduring competitive distance for the businesses they lead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications for Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owned the P&amp;amp;L or revenue number of a B2B SaaS, FinTech, or vertical software business, with direct accountability for revenue growth, retention, and margin expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7–10+ years of senior commercial leadership at a software or technology company, including direct responsibility for selling to, managing, or delivering to wealth managers, private banks, or asset managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in wealth management software or Portfolio Management Systems, or adjacent FinTech / WealthTech. Experience at a direct competitor carries immediate credibility with prospects and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the UK wealth management ecosystem (private banks, discretionary fund managers, IFAs, and External Asset Managers) and existing relationships with key buyers and influencers. Ideally, UK-based or strongly tied to the UK.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has built a go-to-market motion in a new geography: hiring local talent, establishing partnerships, and opening a market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has led an organisation through a meaningful inflexion point, such as a competitive situation, building a business from scratch, pricing repositioning, or commercial professionalisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated AI conviction: shipped product capability, embedded operational tooling, or led sustained AI experimentation with clear conviction about where it creates durable value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable building and leading a local commercial operation within a company of roughly 30 to 80 people in an investor-backed setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to operate entrepreneurially while working within a jointly agreed strategy and governance framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English is essential. French is a significant advantage given the Geneva headquarters and Swiss relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in the UK, ideally within reach of London, and able to commit to regular on-site presence in Geneva.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*Please complete your application and submit your CV in English&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Diversity, Equity, Inclusion &amp;amp; Equal Employment Opportunity at Banyan: Banyan affirms that inequality is detrimental to our Global Teams, associates, our Operating Companies, and the communities we serve. As a collective, our goal is to impact lasting change through our actions. Together, we unite for equality and equity. Banyan is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of any protected characteristic, including race, color, genetic information, creed, national origin, religion, sex, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, lawful alien status, ancestry, age, marital status, or protected veteran status and will not discriminate against anyone on the basis of a disability. We support an inclusive workplace where associates excel based on personal merit, qualifications, experience, ability, and job performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please Note&lt;/strong&gt;: Banyan Software does not accept unsolicited resumes or applications submitted via email, LinkedIn, or other direct channels. All candidates must apply through our official Careers site to be considered for employment. Applications submitted outside of our applicant tracking system will not be reviewed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Notice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Banyan Software may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to assist in screening and/or assessing applicants during the recruitment process. All hiring decisions are made by our team. Personal information submitted through your application will be collected and used for recruitment purposes in accordance with applicable privacy laws. Contact us at any time with questions about our process or to request accommodation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beware of Recruitment Scams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have been made aware of individuals fraudulently posing as members of our Talent Acquisition team and extending fake job offers. These scams may involve requests for personal information or payment for equipment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protect yourself by following these steps:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify that all communications from our recruiting team come from an ----- email address.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remember, employers will &lt;strong&gt;never&lt;/strong&gt; request payment or banking information during the hiring process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you receive a suspicious message, &lt;strong&gt;do not respond&lt;/strong&gt; — instead, forward it to &lt;a ---------- and/or report it to the platform where you received it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your safety and security are important to us. Thank you for staying vigilant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Banyan Software is the best permanent home for software businesses that serve specialized industries, their employees, and their customers. We are on a mission to acquire, build, and grow great companies worldwide, helping them modernize through shared AI expertise and operational discipline. The Banyan Software Foundation, endowed with $100 million in Banyan stock, leverages technology to build a greener and more equitable world. Banyan is Great Place to Work Certified, a five-time Inc. 5000 honoree, and a top 10 company on the Deloitte Technology Fast 500. Founded in 2016 and headquartered in Atlanta, Banyan operates more than 100 portfolio companies across North America, the UK, EU, and APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Recruiter: Europe (Hybrid)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re building a portfolio of exceptional software businesses across the globe. As our European presence continues to expand through acquisitions and organic growth, we’re looking for a seasoned Principal Recruiter to independently lead and execute hiring across all levels, including executive search, across our portfolio companies and headquarters throughout Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible, high-impact role where you’ll operate as a strategic talent partner to CEOs, senior executives, and business leaders. You’ll own searches end-to-end: scoping roles, mapping markets, engaging candidates, and closing hires without needing day-to-day guidance. Beyond individual searches, you’ll help shape how we approach talent across a growing, multi-country portfolio, bringing structure, best practices, and market intelligence that raises the bar for the entire function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you thrive on working autonomously, building trusted relationships with senior leaders, and solving complex hiring challenges across geographies, this is an opportunity to influence growth at both a regional and global level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute recruitment across all levels independently. Lead full-cycle hiring from intake through close, including executive-level searches (C-suite, VP, Managing Director, and other key leadership positions) across our growing European portfolio. You’ll manage your own requisition load, prioritize competing demands, and drive results with minimal oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build proactive, long-term talent pipelines. Continuously map talent landscapes across multiple European markets, identify emerging leaders, and cultivate relationships with high-caliber professionals well before hiring needs arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted talent advisor to senior leaders. Partner directly with CEOs, executives, and leadership teams on talent market trends, organizational design, succession planning, and leadership hiring strategy. You’ll bring a point of view grounded in data and market intelligence, not just fill open roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring structure and rigor to how we hire. Design and implement best-in-class recruiting processes that can be leveraged across portfolio companies, ensuring a consistent, high-quality hiring experience regardless of geography or business unit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data and competitive intelligence. Use market knowledge, compensation benchmarking, and talent analytics to inform hiring decisions and executive search strategies across diverse European geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect talent strategy to business outcomes. Work at the intersection of talent and business strategy, helping portfolio companies secure the leaders and key contributors they need to execute growth plans, drive transformation, and maximize long-term value creation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elevate the broader recruiting function. Share expertise, mentor less experienced team members, and contribute to the development of scalable recruiting playbooks, tools, and standards across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive&amp;nbsp; recruiting experience, with deep expertise in executive search, leadership hiring, and senior-level talent acquisition. You’ve led complex, high-stakes searches and closed senior hires in competitive markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage a complex full requisition load independently.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting across multiple European markets with an understanding of diverse talent landscapes, cultures, labor regulations, and hiring environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building and maintaining proactive executive talent pipelines in fast-paced, high-growth, or multi-business environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen. You connect talent strategy to organizational growth objectives and can speak the language of the business leaders you support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credibility with senior stakeholders. You’ve earned the trust of executives, CEOs, and board-level leaders through data, market intelligence, and strategic insight, not just speed of delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic mindset paired with hands-on execution. You’re equally comfortable advising on org design as you are sourcing a niche candidate in a new market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house executive recruiting experience preferred. Agency or search firm backgrounds are valued, but you should understand the dynamics of partnering with internal stakeholders over time and building long-term relationships inside a growing organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Diversity, Equity, Inclusion &amp;amp; Equal Employment Opportunity at Banyan: Banyan affirms that inequality is detrimental to our Global Teams, associates, our Operating Companies, and the communities we serve. As a collective, our goal is to impact lasting change through our actions. Together, we unite for equality and equity. Banyan is committed to equal employment opportunities regardless of any protected characteristic, including race, color, genetic information, creed, national origin, religion, sex, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, lawful alien status, ancestry, age, marital status, or protected veteran status and will not discriminate against anyone on the basis of a disability. We support an inclusive workplace where associates excel based on personal merit, qualifications, experience, ability, and job performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please Note&lt;/strong&gt;: Banyan Software does not accept unsolicited resumes or applications submitted via email, LinkedIn, or other direct channels. All candidates must apply through our official Careers site to be considered for employment. Applications submitted outside of our applicant tracking system will not be reviewed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Notice&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Banyan Software may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to assist in screening and/or assessing applicants during the recruitment process. All hiring decisions are made by our team. Personal information submitted through your application will be collected and used for recruitment purposes in accordance with applicable privacy laws. Contact us at any time with questions about our process or to request accommodation.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beware of Recruitment Scams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have been made aware of individuals fraudulently posing as members of our Talent Acquisition team and extending fake job offers. These scams may involve requests for personal information or payment for equipment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protect yourself by following these steps:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify that all communications from our recruiting team come from an ----- email address.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remember, employers will &lt;strong&gt;never&lt;/strong&gt; request payment or banking information during the hiring process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you receive a suspicious message, &lt;strong&gt;do not respond&lt;/strong&gt; — instead, forward it to &lt;a ---------- and/or report it to the platform where you received it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your safety and security are important to us. Thank you for staying vigilant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a &quot;normalized&quot; problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Available Location: London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the world’s first connectivity cloud, Cloudflare helps connect and protect millions of customers globally. Everyone from individuals to the world’s largest enterprises use our unified platform of networking, security, and developer services to succeed everywhere in the world. Supporting a global platform of this scale requires a legal team that moves fast. That’s why at Cloudflare, we don’t just manage risk—we clear the road for global innovation. We are building a next generation compliance program that leverages AI technology to scale our routine tasks, allowing our team members to focus on the proactive work of fostering a culture of compliance.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a talented, experienced, and energetic compliance professional&amp;nbsp; to join our legal team as a Senior Ethics and Compliance Manager (EMEA) based in London. You will play a key role executing the day-to-day nuts and bolts of our legal compliance within the EMEA region, including internal investigations, managing conflicts of interest disclosures, gifts and entertainment reviews, legal and compliance training, and project management of cross-functional initiates. Just as importantly, you will be responsible for helping build our systems and processes in a way that leverages AI to allow us to do our best work. The ideal candidate is passionate about compliance and can channel that passion into solving complex problems and novel legal issues in a fast-paced environment. As part of the job, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Cloudflare’s &lt;strong&gt;internal investigations program&lt;/strong&gt;, including management of investigation case files, conducting witness interviews, collecting supporting documentation, and drafting final reports;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design and implement &lt;strong&gt;policies and controls&lt;/strong&gt; to ensure that Cloudflare is protecting its customers and employees, while satisfying our legal obligations;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with Cloudflare’s &lt;strong&gt;conflict of interest disclosure process&lt;/strong&gt;, including review and approval of potential employee conflicts and gift and entertainment requests&lt;strong&gt;;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the administration of Cloudflare’s &lt;strong&gt;compliance training and education program&lt;/strong&gt;, including the design of regional compliance training content, target audience identification and effectiveness measurement;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with execution of a regular integrity and &lt;strong&gt;compliance communications strategy within the region&lt;/strong&gt;; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project manage a variety of other &lt;strong&gt;cross-functional compliance initiatives&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The above list is representative and additional responsibilities may be assigned, as required by the need for the compliance program to support Cloudflare’s Legal team with agility in a dynamic environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of compliance and investigative experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and designing compliance frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest and Enthusiasm for finding ways to implement and leverage AI in compliance functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting and participating in complex investigations and witness interviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with an in-house legal department preferred; experience at a tech company, especially as part of a compliance team, is a huge plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in managing Conflicts of Interest to resolution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General familiarity with the process and requirements of Disciplinary Hearings in EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented, well-organized and technically-adept&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and oral communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the following software tools helpful not not required: Google suite, Navex (EthicsPoint, RiskRate, Disclosures)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills and experience in working cross-functionally with a variety of teams, with lawyers and non-lawyers, including engineering teams, sales teams, and product teams, to establish effective solutions efficiently and in an amenable manner.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to manage multiple matters / projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter with the ability to learn in a fast-paced environment with minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering in-person and/or virtual trainings and workshops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Speaking multiple languages is a bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes Cloudflare Special?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re not just a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company. We’re a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company with a soul. Fundamental to our mission to help build a better Internet is protecting the free and open Internet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.cloudflare.com/protecting-free-expression-online/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Galileo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: Since 2014, we&#39;ve equipped more than 2,400 journalism and civil society organizations in 111 countries with powerful tools to defend themselves against attacks that would otherwise censor their work, technology already used by Cloudflare’s enterprise customers--at no cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudflare.com/athenian/&quot;&gt;Athenian Project&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: In 2017, we created the Athenian Project to ensure that state and local governments have the highest level of protection and reliability for free, so that their constituents have access to election information and voter registration. Since the project, we&#39;ve provided services to more than 425 local government election websites in 33 states.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://1.1.1.1/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.1.1.1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: We released&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://1.1.1.1/&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;1.1.1.1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to help fix the foundation of the Internet by building a faster, more secure and privacy-centric public DNS resolver. This is available publicly for everyone to use - it is the first consumer-focused service Cloudflare has ever released. Here’s the deal - we don’t store client IP addresses never, ever. We will continue to abide by our&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/1.1.1.1/privacy/public-dns-resolver&quot;&gt; privacy commitment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; and ensure that no user data is sold to advertisers or used to target consumers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Sound like something you’d like to be a part of? We’d love to hear from you!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Please note that applicants who progress to the offer stage of the interview process may be asked to attend an in-person interview within one of the Cloudflare Offices or Cloudflare Hubs.&amp;nbsp; More details about this will be available at that stage of the interview process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This position may require access to information protected under U.S. export control laws, including the U.S. Export Administration Regulations. Please note that any offer of employment may be conditioned on your authorization to receive software or technology controlled under these U.S. export laws without sponsorship for an export license.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Cloudflare is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. &amp;nbsp;We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity for all people and place great value in both diversity and inclusiveness. &amp;nbsp;All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to their, or any other person&#39;s, perceived or actual&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, physical or mental disability, medical condition, family care status, or any other basis protected by law. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are an AA/Veterans/Disabled Employer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Cloudflare provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. &amp;nbsp;Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job. Examples of reasonable accommodations include, but are not limited to, changing the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. &amp;nbsp;If you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job, please contact us via e-mail at &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: ----- style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; or via mail at 101 Townsend St. San Francisco, CA 94107.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;The Storage Layer Services team is currently re-architecting the MongoDB Cloud Storage Layer. This is a relatively new team in MongoDB that sits at the heart of the next generation MongoDB Cloud Storage Architecture, and the team is working to build performant multi-tenant distributed storage services both to enhance our existing MongoDB cloud storage architecture and to power more of our customers&#39; use cases more efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering at MongoDB is globally distributed, with a mix of folks being fully remote, hybrid, or in-office. We have a small but growing team that calls Sydney home, and we are looking for a Staff Engineer to join the team working closely with other teams in Sydney and North America.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team champions a strong culture of inclusivity, diversity, and collaboration. If you want to work on a collaborative team that applies great engineering fundamentals to deliver core features of a popular database, join us! Let’s change what’s possible for application developers, system architects, and database operators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to speak to candidates who are based in Sydney for our hybrid working model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You’re an ideal candidate if:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 10+ years of experience in programming, debugging, and performance tuning highly concurrent and/or distributed systems. Especially if you have worked in a systems language (C, C++, Rust, etc) for a number of those years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record as an effective technical leader. You love helping teams be successful at solving vaguely defined problems in iterative and measurable ways. You put the customer first, and don’t hesitate to cross team boundaries in search of the right solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a solid grasp of related systems fundamentals, such as cache management, log-based recovery, transactions or performance profiling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable reasoning about highly concurrent, asynchronous services — backpressure, tail latency, and the failure modes of replicated state machines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve worked on large, highly available, scalable and performant systems such as databases, high frequency trading platforms, cloud storage services, or maybe even Mars rovers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have excellent verbal and written technical communication skills; you enjoy collaborating with colleagues and mentoring junior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy learning new things in the domains of computer science and software engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;As a Staff Engineer on the Storage Layer Services team you will:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be directly responsible for delivering on goals which span a 6-18 month timeframe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play a key role in defining the roadmap for the next 12 months&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write well tested, production-ready code in rust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a force multiplier across the organization, drive improvements to processes and tools to help us more confidently make sound decisions and&amp;nbsp; changes to high risk parts of our codebase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use our observability stack to inform decisions and measure the impact of work the team ships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate performance regressions and guide the team through making complex changes that have to balance performance against other requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a culture of operational excellence, and be part of a one-week-in-6 on-call rotation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help cultivate a strong talent bench through interviewing, mentoring and knowledge sharing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain and apply expertise on cutting edge database and distributed systems research from industry and academia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle (or lead the effort to handle) time-sensitive customer escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and advocate for high-impact projects across teams, connecting customer needs and company goals to a clear technical strategy for large initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive consensus on abstract, complex issues affecting multiple teams by framing tradeoffs, engaging stakeholders, and guiding decisions to durable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be open to occasional (once a year) travel to the US&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Success Measures:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the first month:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have understood the high level architecture of SLS and fixed a few bugs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are starting to develop relationships with key stakeholders across your VPs organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In three months:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have diagnosed and fixed a few customer or testing-reported issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have contributed to the development of SLS and shipped your first feature to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are starting to take on code review responsibilities and are involved in reviewing the design for new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In six months:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have started mentoring other engineers on the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are leading the development of a new feature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are beginning to involve yourself in planning and roadmapping efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In twelve months:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have successfully shipped multiple major contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You own a department level goal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 weeks annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;22 weeks paid parental leave for both parents that covers childbirth, adoption, surrogacy and fostering. In your first year with MongoDB this benefit is reduced&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family forming assistance which covers fertility care, adoption and surrogacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidised health &amp;amp; dental insurance for you and your dependents (through Medibank)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Classpass credits, a Headspace subscription and Vaccination vouchers as part of our broader health and wellness programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office Lunch (on us) up to 3 days per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About MongoDB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified data platform, the most widely available, globally distributed data platform on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud data platform and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With offices worldwide and over 67,000 customers, including 75% of the Fortune 100 and AI-native startups, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compass at MongoDB is our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company&quot;&gt;Leadership Commitment,&lt;/a&gt; guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To drive the personal growth and business impact of our employees, we’re committed to developing a supportive and enriching culture for everyone. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/culture/employee-benefits-that-make-a-difference-at-mongodb&quot;&gt;From employee affinity groups, to fertility assistance and a generous parental leave policy&lt;/a&gt;, we value our employees’ wellbeing and want to support them along every step of their professional and personal journeys.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/blog/channel/culture&quot;&gt; Learn more about what it’s like to work at MongoDB&lt;/a&gt;, and help us make an impact on the world!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is committed to providing any necessary accommodations for individuals with disabilities within our application and interview process. To request an accommodation due to a disability, please inform your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is an equal opportunities employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;fields&quot;&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
