At Crytek we're building a scalable UI platform powered by a Design System implemented in Coherent Gameface (HTML, CSS, JavaScript).
Instead of building UI screen-by-screen, we are creating reusable components and architecture that power Hunt: Showdown and future Crytek titles.
We’re looking for a Senior Web Design Engineer&nbsp;to help build this system - translating Figma components into production-ready UI and shaping how UI is developed across Crytek.
This is an opportunity to build the UI foundation for multiple games, not just individual screens.
We welcome candidates from a variety of backgrounds and experiences who are excited about building thoughtful, scalable UI.
This position is based in Frankfurt, Germany.
An online portfolio with updated work samples is necessary. Your 
portfolio should demonstrate the following:

The scope of your contribution on each project
Visual polish and attention to detail
A strong sense of UX, both in your work and how your portfolio itself is organized
Clean, well-structured code
Thoughtful use of modular UI components
What you'll Do

Build&nbsp;reusable UI components using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript
Implement&nbsp;scalable UI architecture using Coherent Gameface
Translate&nbsp;Figma design system components into production-ready UI
Assemble UI screens from&nbsp;reusable components
Improve the&nbsp;design to development pipeline, including tooling and workflows
Collaborate with&nbsp;UX, UI art, and engineering to deliver a modern UI pipeline
Help define and scale the&nbsp;UI platform used across future Crytek projects

What you bring
Experience in web or UI engineering (rough guideline: ~5+ years, but we value equivalent practical experience)
Strong skills in HTML5, CSS, and JavaScript
Experience with games, Figma, or AI-assisted workflows
Experience with Web Components and a major frontend framework (React, Vue, Svelte etc.)
Experience building&nbsp;component-based UI systems
Good understanding of&nbsp;UI architecture and performance
Passionate about games and player experiences, with an appreciation for how great UI and UX contribute to gameplay across all genres.
Experience collaborating closely with&nbsp;design teams
Willingness to relocate to Frankfurt am Main, Germany.&nbsp;
What you can expect from us
Career Path&nbsp;
Your professional development is important to us, so we have laid out a career plan to help you progress towards your goals and objectives.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Relocation&nbsp;Support&nbsp;
We offer a relocation budget and full coverage of flights to Frankfurt for you and your family.&nbsp;
You can expect extensive assistance with visa, work permits, and communication with authorities during the relocation process, as well as help settling into Germany (e.g. setting up appointments with banks, government agencies, schools, landlords, finding apartments etc.).
&nbsp;
Company Apartment&nbsp;
To help you get settled, we provide you with a fully furnished company apartment during your first three months in Frankfurt.
&nbsp;
Public Transport Pass&nbsp;
Discover Frankfurt by bus, tram and metro – free of charge.
&nbsp;
Gym Card&nbsp;
A healthy body is a healthy mind. We offer a membership at the premium gym chain Fitness First in Germany. Work out, join group fitness classes, or relax in the wellness facilities.
&nbsp;
State-of-the-art Office
We’ve recently moved into a brand-new, modern office located in the heart of Frankfurt. Our new workspace is designed to inspire creativity and collaboration, with open areas, quiet zones, and top-tier facilities — all just steps away from public transport, restaurants, bars and cultural hotspots.
&nbsp;
Hybrid WorkingWe believe in the value of in-person collaboration while also supporting flexibility. Our hybrid working model includes three days per week in the office and the option to work remotely up to two days per week, unless role-specific requirements or business needs require you to be on site.
&nbsp;
Equal Opportunity &amp; Inclusion
We’re building a workplace where everyone belongs. We welcome people of all backgrounds and identities and are proud to be a truly global team, with employees from over 42 countries contributing their ideas, cultures, and perspectives every day.
&nbsp;
German Classes&nbsp;
Understanding the local culture will make your stay abroad more enjoyable, and Crytek supports that by offering German language courses for you and your family.&nbsp;
&nbsp;&nbsp;
Events
Join us on our exciting company events, including new starter breakfasts, summer and winter parties, our annual trip to Gamescom in Cologne, and many more!
&nbsp;
Vacation Days&nbsp;
At our Frankfurt office you can enjoy 24 days of vacation per year, and every 2 years you get 1 more (up to a maximum of 28 days). You will also have on average 10 public holidays on top of the days you take off.&nbsp;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

We are looking for an experienced and talented Senior Tools Engineer for our CRYENGINE&nbsp;Tools team at our new state-of-the-art office in Frankfurt, Germany.
As a Senior Tools Engineer, you will be working in a cooperative, cross-disciplinary environment to develop industry-leading tools, contributing to the improvement of productivity and quality for game teams and the CRYENGINE Sandbox Editor. As part of our innovative and ambitious team, you can expect your abilities and scope of duties to grow as you make a real difference.
What You'll Do

Help create and deploy our suite of development tools, both in-cloud and on-prem, across multiple platforms.
Contribute to the development of the CRYENGINE Sandbox Editor.
Collaborate closely with artists, designers, and software engineers on the requirements and design of tools.
Propose tools and methods to increase the efficiency and quality of content development.
Contribute to maintenance and improvements of critical low-level systems.
Ensure reliability and stability of the code base, and drive adoption of new techniques, technologies and languages.

What You Will Deliver

5+ years of relevant professional software development experience.
Excellent C#, C++ programming skills.
Experience with distributed, micro-service architectures and software configuration and deployment with Kubernetes.
Experience developing user interfaces and working with HTML and Qt frameworks (or similar).
Expertise with performance profiling tools.
Willing to relocate to Frankfurt am Main area, Germany.

Nice To Have (Not Required) 

Experience working with multithreaded, real-time systems.
Knowledge of WPF and/or TSX (e.g. React)
Strong TypeScript, Python, Rust, Go programming skills.
Experience with any game Engines preferably experience with CRYENGINE.

